Quoted spans:
```python
QUOTE_PAIRS = [('"','"'),("'","'"),("“","”"),("‘","’"),("«","»")]
def quoted_spans(t):
    spans=[]
    for a,b in QUOTE_PAIRS:
        i=0
        while True:
            i=t.find(a,i)
            if i<0: break
            j=t.find(b,i+1)
            if j<0: break
            spans.append((i,j+1)); i=j+1
    return spans
```
(apostrophes in "R1's" handled by requiring the opening quote to be preceded by start/space/punct in the single-quote case.)

